  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "By 2024, AARO, the Pentagon office that now looks into reports of unexplained objects in the sky, had a staff of roughly three to four dozen people, and that week it had been declared at full operational capability. The commentator Marik von Rennenkampff says this, without naming a source, and links it to the office's director, Jon Kosloski, its pile of about 1,600 cases, and how puzzled its own leadership is by some of them. He raises it to show how small the government's effort is next to the size of the question."
